1102:| OD111 | <a id="od111"></a>Misaligned fields of a packed struct (added 2026-10-30, from the Codex and Kimi review of the absorption). Question: Whether a `#[repr(packed)]` struct may hold a field whose alignment exceeds the alignment of its offset, and whether such a field may be borrowed. Bears on FFI-4, FFI-8, REF-5. The current compiler: both accepted: `#[repr(packed)] struct P { v: u8, l: u32 }` places `l` at offset 1, and `&p.l` is accepted and reads the field correctly in the binary and in `--interp`. [LAYOUT_CONTRACT.md](../legacy/docs/archive/design-records/LAYOUT_CONTRACT.md) §2 restricts a packed struct to fields whose alignment does not exceed their position, without saying what enforces it. Options: (a) refuse such a field; (b) accept it and refuse a reference to it; (c) accept both, as in the current compiler. Austral: not checked. Pick: none given (raised by the Codex and Kimi review of the absorption, 2026-10-30). | both accepted on both consumers | FFI-4, FFI-8, REF-5 | decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Accept field, refuse a reference to it |
