codex
**A — DISAGREE as written.** Agree with compact native tags, declaration-order numbering and deferring niches. Specify payload alignment, padding and invalid-tag handling too. C-compatible enums must follow the selected target’s C ABI; `i32` is not a universal FFI rule. Compact native tags would revise [OD126](docs/decisions.md#od126), which decided the existing profile’s assumptions as language rules. Recommend the revision, subject to owner approval.

**B — AGREE.** Erase release context when release needs no per-instance information and its operation is statically known. A single allocator alone does not establish that condition. Stateful allocators retain sufficient stable context, with lifetime dependencies checked. This fits [Q1.7](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core): stable release state and raw context, without safe references. Embedded programs then pay only for metadata they actually need.

**C — DISAGREE as explained.** The conditional representation rule is good; the examples confuse capabilities with grants. `with(Console)` or `with(Entropy)` expresses permission; a grant may select a stream, device, rights or lifecycle state. Erase a grant only when that information is statically determined and erasure preserves authority and linear consumption. Allocators follow the same rule. Treating every grant as pure permission would conflict with the decided [grant model](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core).

**KEPT — AGREE, with qualifications.** These are predictable defaults for both environments. Make lengths target-sized and layout arithmetic checked; zero-sized values still need defined alignment, addressing and array behavior. `Secret<T>` sharing `T`’s layout does not itself establish constant time. Item 6 conflicts with [OD126](docs/decisions.md#od126) unless other targets remain explicitly separate profiles or the owner revises it. Declaration-order structs already match the newer [layout decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-runtime-2026-11-06).

**GAP — DISAGREE with calling all three undecided candidates.** [OD111](docs/decisions.md#od111) already accepts misaligned packed fields while refusing references to them; [OD147](docs/decisions.md#od147) accepts C-order packing with alignment 1. Preserve those decisions while scheduling implementation. Workload-driven timing is sensible, but MMIO needs explicit access widths and observable access semantics before a device workload ships. Volatile access must not implicitly promise atomicity or hardware ordering.

**OTHER — CHANGE the target model, not the defaults.** Model address width, pointer storage/alignment, length width and address spaces separately; an 8-bit MCU need not have 8-bit pointers. Resolve the decided raw-pointer model’s `addr: u64` ([Q3.7](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core)) explicitly. For servers, support explicit stronger alignment for SIMD, caches and atomics when workloads require it. Keep packing opt-in and field order explicit; avoid automatic reordering or speculative niche rules.

ANSWER: A=DISAGREE; B=AGREE; C=DISAGREE; KEPT=AGREE; GAP=DISAGREE; OTHER=CHANGE
